From d33e982e5b74aeffe34dd0328c4dea2ec9b71b9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 18:29:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] param: don't deny every app write on products without
 SELinux

OpenHarmony-7.0 added, for builds without PARAM_SUPPORT_SELINUX, a
blanket PARAM_CODE_PERMISSION_DENIED for any caller with
uid >= PUBLIC_APP_BEGIN_UID.  Apps are not DAC-checked (their uids are
per-bundle), so with SELinux the policy is the only gate; without
SELinux there is no gate at all and the new rule turns every app write
into a refusal.

That breaks boot on such products: SystemUI's screen lock and the
launcher announce themselves through bootevent.lockscreen.ready and
bootevent.launcher.ready, init logs "Forbid to set parameter ...", and
bootevent.boot.completed is never set.

Restore the OpenHarmony-6.1 behaviour for non-SELinux builds; SELinux
builds are unchanged.

Change-Id: I6be081981f65e537bd74544f676965a49d00539b
Signed-off-by: Francesco Pham <francesco.pham1@h-partners.com>
---
 services/param/base/param_base.c | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/param/base/param_base.c b/services/param/base/param_base.c
index 4d22b520e..c40f7726b 100644
--- a/services/param/base/param_base.c
+++ b/services/param/base/param_base.c
@@ -609,10 +609,6 @@ static int CheckParamPermission_(const ParamLabelIndex *labelIndex,
     if (ret == DAC_RESULT_PERMISSION) {
         ret = SelinuxCheckParamPermission(labelIndex, srcLabel, name, mode);
     }
-#else
-    if (srcLabel->cred.uid >= PUBLIC_APP_BEGIN_UID) {
-        ret = PARAM_CODE_PERMISSION_DENIED;
-    }
 #endif
     return ret;
 }
